+## Enabling and disabling CDC
+
+You don't have to decide on CDC when you create the source. Open the source's **Configuration** tab to enable, monitor, and disable CDC at any time without deleting and recreating the source (which would lose your schedule and schema history).
+
+- **Enable CDC** – PostHog re-runs the prerequisite checks against your database, provisions the CDC resources, and sets up the extraction schedule. You choose the management mode (see below) and, for self-managed mode, the publication name. Enabling fails if CDC is already enabled, or if a replication slot or publication with the chosen name already exists.
+- **Monitor CDC** – The Configuration tab shows whether the replication slot and publication currently exist on your database, plus the current WAL lag.
+- **Update CDC settings** – After CDC is enabled you can change automatic slot protection and the WAL lag warning and critical thresholds. The warning threshold must be lower than the critical threshold. The management mode, slot name, and publication name are fixed once CDC is enabled; to change them, disable CDC and enable it again.
+- **Disable CDC** – PostHog cancels any running CDC syncs, removes the extraction schedule, drops the CDC resources it owns (see the modes below), and soft-deletes the `_cdc` history tables. CDC schemas are paused and must pick a new sync method before they sync again. Re-enabling CDC starts from a clean state.
+
 ## Slot and publication management
 
 PostHog supports two CDC management modes.
